A 'short' little announcement about the nethack yani database. It's still
at http://student.bvsd.k12.co.us/~schoonov/yani/yani.cgi, but I've
rewritten all of its code from scratch.

I had left it alone for the last couple of months, but recently I went back
and added some YANIs.  In the process, I discovered my code had some icky
portability problems.  It was written in C, and something went wrong on the
Solaris box where it worked fine on my FreeBSD box (some troubles with
malloc it looks like...ew).

I ended up rewriting it from scratch in perl (oddly enough, I started with
that language in the first place way back in April, but gave up because I
didn't know the language well enough), and made the code much happier. 
It took almost 6000 lines in C, and then had to have a compiled binary.  In
perl, it only takes up 1234 lines.  The means we can have more YANIs in the
database before my quota runs out. 

This all means it's going to get updated more frequently (again).  And more
YASDs on my part, since I've gotten readdicted to NetHack. :P

